Comment: 50,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.02,Default,chptr,0,0,0,,{Intro}
Comment: 50,0:00:05.82,0:00:05.86,Default,chptr,0,0,0,,{The Cattle Museum, Part 2}
Comment: 50,0:04:09.20,0:04:09.23,Default,chptr,0,0,0,,{Credits}
Dialogue: 50,0:00:05.82,0:00:10.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Continuing where we left off\Nat the Cattle Museum...
Dialogue: 50,0:00:10.36,0:00:13.16,Default,,0,0,0,,When we think of livestock cattle,\Nwe picture the Holstein,
Dialogue: 50,0:00:13.16,0:00:15.97,Default,,0,0,0,,but their ancestor actually looked like this: the aurochs!
Dialogue: 50,0:00:15.97,0:00:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Geez, that's huge!\NAnd some were even close to 2 meters tall?
Dialogue: 50,0:00:18.50,0:00:22.61,Default,,0,0,0,,These wild cattle were depicted\Nin cave paintings 15,000 years ago,
Dialogue: 50,0:00:22.61,0:00:26.84,Default,,0,0,0,,and it's believed that capturing one then\Nwas a coming of age test.
Dialogue: 50,0:00:26.84,0:00:29.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Must've been pretty violent\Nas wild animals.
Dialogue: 50,0:00:29.15,0:00:34.85,Default,,0,0,0,,What could have led humanity to capture,\Ndomesticate, and breed these wild giant beasts anyways?
Dialogue: 50,0:00:34.85,0:00:36.72,Default,,0,0,0,,They must have been very delicious.
Dialogue: 50,0:00:36.72,0:00:39.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Humanity's pursuit of food is admirable.
Dialogue: 50,0:00:45.36,0:00:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,The wild cattle gave way to many breeds\Nbased on the region, era, and culture.
Dialogue: 50,0:00:50.33,0:00:53.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Cattle around the world\Ncome in many shapes and sizes!
Dialogue: 50,0:00:53.70,0:00:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,They look so colorful altogether!
Dialogue: 50,0:00:55.71,0:01:01.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly! Their varying coat colors\Nare a distinct trait of their domestication!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:01.35,0:01:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}On the other hand, wild cattle's coats\Nare duller so they blend into their natural surroundings.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:06.15,0:01:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ah, since animals that stand out\Nare easier targets!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:09.22,0:01:13.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}But when humans keep them,\Nthey're swayed by the variations,
Dialogue: 50,0:01:13.22,0:01:15.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}and try to maintain that breed.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:15.26,0:01:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Oh, that checks out.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:16.43,0:01:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}My friend's ranch found the brown Holsteins so cute,\Nthey bred them with other ones to keep them around.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:22.20,0:01:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So what makes animals easy or difficult to domesticate?
Dialogue: 50,0:01:26.17,0:01:28.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd say it's whether or not\Nthey behave like weeds.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:28.61,0:01:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Animals that domesticate best are ones\Nthat can easily adapt to their environment.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:32.54,0:01:34.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, I'm pretty chill wherever.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:34.65,0:01:37.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'm sure you'll make great livestock.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:37.15,0:01:40.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that Arakawa has found her new calling...
Dialogue: 50,0:01:40.42,0:01:44.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's speed through the other exhibits\Nin the Cattle Museum!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:44.62,0:01:46.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Cow coins from all over the world!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:46.66,0:01:48.86,Default,,0,0,0,,The English word "cattle"
Dialogue: 50,0:01:48.86,0:01:53.36,Default,,0,0,0,,is actually derived from the late Latin "captale",\Nwhich means "capital" or "property".
Dialogue: 50,0:01:53.36,0:01:55.90,Default,,0,0,0,,That explains all the cow money!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:55.90,0:01:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the specimen of a cow stomach!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:57.94,0:01:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,That's huge!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:58.50,0:02:01.77,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a Jersey cattle stomach.\NHolsteins' are {\i1}way{\i0} bigger.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:01.77,0:02:04.34,Default,,0,0,0,,There's also exhibits for cowbells,
Dialogue: 50,0:02:04.34,0:02:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,milk cans, cow toys, cow festivals,
Dialogue: 50,0:02:07.54,0:02:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,and all sorts of other cow things\Nfrom all over the world.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:10.48,0:02:15.02,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's not all!\NHere's one exhibit Arakawa and Ishii got to see...
Dialogue: 50,0:02:15.02,0:02:17.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa! So this is a coffin!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:17.59,0:02:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,They have cattle and pig molds!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:20.16,0:02:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Pigs, a representation of fecundity, were used for women,\Nwhile water buffalos were used for men.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:25.70,0:02:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,The Torajan revered water buffaloes\Nand believed they guided the souls of the dead.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:31.30,0:02:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Interesting! I'm a woman,\Nbut I'd love to be buried in the cow coffin.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:35.74,0:02:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand, but one problem—\Nthe Torajan did {\i1}wind{\i0} burials.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:39.28,0:02:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:39.71,0:02:43.51,Default,,0,0,0,,The coffin would be left outdoors\Nto be exposed to the elements,
Dialogue: 50,0:02:43.51,0:02:47.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and it's believed that the coffin\Nwould break, causing the skull to fall out,
Dialogue: 50,0:02:47.35,0:02:50.15,Default,,0,0,0,,and kids would start playing soccer with it.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:50.15,0:02:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:54.49,0:02:56.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Hey, look at this Noble Farmer!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:56.66,0:02:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Golly, that's one fine Noble Farmer!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:59.23,0:03:01.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you two for taking the tour!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:01.60,0:03:03.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you enjoy the exhibits?
Dialogue: 50,0:03:03.17,0:03:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It was very educational!\NI appreciate the detailed explanations you gave!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:07.81,0:03:09.87,Default,,0,0,0,,We had a very cow-ful day!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:09.87,0:03:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,One last thing, Morimoto-san!\NGive us your top recommendation for this museum!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:13.88,0:03:16.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah! What's the thing people've {\i1}gotta{\i0} see?
Dialogue: 50,0:03:16.28,0:03:19.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me think! My top recommendation\Nwould have to be...
Dialogue: 50,0:03:19.95,0:03:22.12,Default,,0,0,0,,the cow stomach!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:22.12,0:03:23.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Of all things?!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:23.02,0:03:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We're selling cow stomach t-shirts\Nin the museum shop, if you're looking for a souvenir!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:28.46,0:03:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You're capitalizing on it?!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:29.79,0:03:31.90,Default,,0,0,0,,You really love that stomach, huh? Sold!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:31.90,0:03:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,With its vast collection of cattle exhibits\Nand its avant-garde merchandise,
Dialogue: 50,0:03:35.50,0:03:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,this place serves to remind us of the connections\Nwe all have to cattle—both as our livelihood and as living beings.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:41.87,0:03:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,And it's none other than the Cattle Museum.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:44.64,0:03:48.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, all of those cattle exhibits\Nmade me hungry.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:48.41,0:03:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Then let's get some Maesawa beef\Nbefore we go!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:50.68,0:03:53.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, we have some recommended places\Nfor Maesawa beef!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:53.45,0:03:55.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The list of stores is mixed in\Nwith the exhibits!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:55.72,0:03:58.02,Default,,0,0,0,,This museum really is crazy for cattle!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:58.02,0:04:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It's community-based\Nand it's eccentric!
Dialogue: 50,0:04:00.52,0:04:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The Cattle Museum in Oshu, Iwate!
Dialogue: 50,0:04:04.13,0:04:07.97,Default,,0,0,0,,We look forward to seeing you there!
